<article class="env-lemma" id="09H2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09H2">Lemma <span data-tag="09H2">9.12.3</span>.</a> Let $K/E/F$ be a tower of algebraic field extensions. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $\alpha \in K$ is separable over $F$, then $\alpha $ is separable over $E$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $K$ is separable over $F$, then $K$ is separable over $E$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will use Lemma <a href="/tag/09H0" data-tag="09H0">9.12.1</a> without further mention. Let $P$ be the minimal polynomial of $\alpha $ over $F$. Let $Q$ be the minimal polynomial of $\alpha $ over $E$. Then $Q$ divides $P$ in the polynomial ring $E[x]$, say $P = QR$. Then $P' = Q'R + QR'$. Thus if $Q' = 0$, then $Q$ divides $P$ and $P'$ hence $P' = 0$ by the lemma. This proves (1). Part (2) follows immediately from (1) and the definitions. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>